  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Soft hands – pass and receive in three steps",
  "description": "Three short steps for 6–8 year olds that the whole group works through in one session, about a minute per step with quick changes in between. Everyone has a ball.\n\nStep 1: players spread out along the boards, pass against the boards and receive their own pass. The ball should roll along the floor. Move closer or further away so the pass needs a different weight. Step 2: put a cone between the player and the boards. Pass on one side of the cone so the ball comes back on the other side: pass on the forehand, receive on the backhand, then the other way round. Step 3: players work in pairs, three to four metres apart, with two cones close together in the middle. Pass past the cones on one side. The partner receives, drags the ball across to the other side and passes back past the cones there.\n\nSet up step 3 while the children do steps 1 and 2. If dragging the ball across is hard: receive on the forehand, move the feet to the other side and pass straight across. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The ball should roll – that matters more than speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Cushion the ball as you receive, do not just hit it."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Match the weight of the pass to the distance."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Ball beside the body, not far in front – otherwise it lifts."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
